<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:course xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="GEOL 143" href="schedule/2011/fall/GEOL/143.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2011" href="schedule/2011.xml">2011</calendarYear><term id="120118" href="schedule/2011/fall.xml">Fall 2011</term><subject id="GEOL" href="schedule/2011/fall/GEOL.xml">Geology</subject></parents><label>History of Life</label><description>Evolution of life from its beginning, illustrating changing faunas and floras through time; the invasion of land and of the skies; the effects of a changing atmosphere, changing climates, and continental drift. Emphasis on dinosaur evolution, ecology, and extinction; also other vertebrates, including mammal-like reptiles, mammals, and the emergence of humans, as well as plants and invertebrates. Same as ESE 143. </description><creditHours>3 hours.</creditHours><sectionDegreeAttributes>Life Sciences course.</sectionDegreeAttributes><genEdCategories><category id="NAT"><description>Natural Sciences &amp; Technology</description><ns2:genEdAttributes><genEdAttribute code="1LS">Nat Sci &amp; Tech - Life Sciences</genEdAttribute></ns2:genEdAttributes></category></genEdCategories><sections><section id="37557" href="schedule/2011/fall/GEOL/143/37557.xml">AB2</section><section id="37558" href="schedule/2011/fall/GEOL/143/37558.xml">AB3</section><section id="37560" href="schedule/2011/fall/GEOL/143/37560.xml">AB4</section><section id="48936" href="schedule/2011/fall/GEOL/143/48936.xml">AB6</section><section id="48935" href="schedule/2011/fall/GEOL/143/48935.xml">AB7</section><section id="37565" href="schedule/2011/fall/GEOL/143/37565.xml">ABA</section><section id="37574" href="schedule/2011/fall/GEOL/143/37574.xml">AL1</section></sections></ns2:course>